{"name":"Oslo Grey","hex":"#878d91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oslo","blocks":[{"text":"Oslo is the capital and largest city of Norway. It constitutes both a county and a municipality. The municipality of Oslo had a population of 724,290 in 2025, while the city's greater urban area had a population of 1,110,887 in 2025, and the metropolitan area had an estimated population of 1,546,706 in 2021."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Nationaltheatret_evening.jpg/330px-Nationaltheatret_evening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oslo","wikidata":"Q585"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Bj%C3%B8rvika_-_Oslo%2C_Norway_2020-12-23.jpg/500px-Bj%C3%B8rvika_-_Oslo%2C_Norway_2020-12-23.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Bj%C3%B8rvika_-_Oslo%2C_Norway_2020-12-23.jpg/1280px-Bj%C3%B8rvika_-_Oslo%2C_Norway_2020-12-23.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th